codex
The synthetic check shows one real robustness issue: the aggressive first-layer variance beta can go negative at small sample tiers. The official baseline didn’t fail, so I’ll treat that as a robustness guard rather than a score-improving change unless a blackbox run confirms it.
codex
Next I’m testing moment-matching constants locally. These alter predictions even when the sample count stays fixed, so they are more likely to matter than small fraction changes that do not cross a power-of-two boundary.
